# Line endings.
#
# Git converts LF to CRLF on checkout under Windows' default `core.autocrlf`.
# That is fine for source, and fatal for a fixture that asserts exact bytes:
# `fixtures/git-log/mixed.log.txt` is a captured `git log` stream in which the
# newline is a *separator between a commit header and its diff*, not text. A
# CRLF checkout leaves a stray CR on the end of every subject, and the parser
# tests fail on Windows in ten places that all look like parser bugs.
#
# `-text` means "never convert this file's line endings, in either direction".
fixtures/git-log/*.log.txt -text

# The extractor goldens are compared byte-for-byte too.
fixtures/**/expected-facts.ndjson -text
